  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 249 AM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nUpper level ridging keeps temperatures above average and near 100F \nfor most locations through Wednesday and Thursday. Overnight lows \nwill remain above normal as well with most in the low to mid 70s \nwith the higher terrain dipping into the 60s. The ridge begins to \nshift eastward and weaken by the end of the week and into this \nweekend. Temperatures move down just a few degrees and remain above \nnormal. It does allow for isolated showers and storms to develop \nover the higher terrain. Rain amounts will be low overall, but very \nisolated spots may end up with an afternoon/evening downpour leading \nto higher amounts.  \n\n-Stickney",
